UPDATE policies SET title = 'Terms & Conditions', body = $seek_terms$
Effective date: 16 October 2026

1. About SEEK
SEEK is an online marketplace operated by BSN Consulting Limited ("SEEK", "we", "us" or "our") in Nigeria. SEEK enables customers to discover and order products offered by independent retailers. Unless a listing expressly says otherwise, the retailer—not SEEK—is the seller and supplier of the product. SEEK provides marketplace technology, order administration and payment coordination.

2. Acceptance and eligibility
By accessing SEEK, creating an account or placing an order, you agree to these Terms and the linked Privacy, Delivery, Returns & Refunds and Prohibited Products policies. If you do not agree, do not use the service. You must be legally capable of entering into a binding agreement. You must provide accurate account, contact and delivery details and keep your login credentials secure.

3. Retailers and product information
Retailers are responsible for their product descriptions, prices, stock, authenticity, quality, safety, warranties and legal compliance. We take reasonable steps to review listings, but a listing or retailer's presence on SEEK is not a guarantee of product quality or endorsement. Product images and colours may vary by device; material differences must be disclosed by the retailer.

4. Orders and prices
Product availability and prices may change until an order is accepted. An order is not confirmed as paid until payment has been verified by the payment provider and SEEK's systems. A payment redirect or screenshot alone is not proof of payment. The checkout total, including disclosed delivery charges and applicable taxes, is the amount payable. If a material pricing or availability error occurs, we may contact you to correct it or cancel and refund the affected order.

5. Payments, cancellations and refunds
Payments are processed through Paystack or another payment method expressly offered at checkout. Customers pay through SEEK's checkout; SEEK coordinates retailer settlement under its retailer arrangements. Cancellation availability depends on order and fulfilment status. Refund requests are handled under the Returns & Refunds Policy and applicable law. Nothing in these Terms removes mandatory consumer rights.

6. Delivery
Delivery may be handled by SEEK, a retailer or a delivery partner. The responsible party, estimated delivery window and charges will be shown where available. Estimates are not guarantees unless expressly stated. See the Delivery Policy.

7. Acceptable use
You must not misuse the platform, submit false information, interfere with security, attempt unauthorised access, manipulate reviews or payments, infringe intellectual property, harass others, or use SEEK for unlawful transactions. We may investigate reports, restrict listings, suspend accounts or cancel transactions where reasonably necessary and lawful.

8. Intellectual property and user content
SEEK's platform, branding and original content are protected by applicable intellectual-property laws. You retain rights in content you submit, but grant SEEK a limited, non-exclusive licence to host, display and use it as needed to operate, promote and secure the marketplace. You must have the rights and permissions needed to submit it.

9. Complaints and disputes
Contact Support@barristerstreet.org with your order reference and a description of the issue. SEEK will review marketplace complaints and may request evidence from the customer, retailer or delivery partner. We aim to resolve complaints fairly, without limiting a person's right to approach a competent regulator or court.

10. Liability and legal rights
To the extent permitted by law, SEEK is not responsible for a retailer's independent acts or omissions beyond obligations imposed on SEEK by law or by its own commitments. Nothing in these Terms excludes liability that cannot lawfully be excluded, misrepresents a consumer's rights, or prevents statutory remedies under Nigerian law.

11. Changes, suspension and termination
We may update these Terms for legal, operational or product changes. We will publish the revised version and update the effective date. Material changes will not retrospectively remove accrued rights. We may suspend or terminate access for serious or repeated breaches, fraud, security risks or legal requirements, with notice where reasonably practicable.

12. Governing law
These Terms are governed by the laws of the Federal Republic of Nigeria. Any dispute is subject to the jurisdiction of competent Nigerian courts, without prejudice to mandatory consumer protections.

Marketplace operator: BSN Consulting Limited. Support: Support@barristerstreet.org.

This document should be reviewed by a qualified Nigerian lawyer before public launch.
$seek_terms$, updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'terms';

UPDATE policies SET title = 'Privacy Policy', body = $seek_privacy$
Effective date: 16 October 2026

1. Who is responsible
SEEK is operated by BSN Consulting Limited ("we", "us" or "SEEK"). This policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, retain and protect personal data when you browse, register, buy, sell, contact support or otherwise use SEEK. Contact: Support@barristerstreet.org.

2. Information we may collect
Depending on how you use SEEK, we may collect account and contact details (such as name, email, phone number and login identifiers); delivery details; order, payment-reference, refund and transaction records; retailer business, verification and payout information; product listings and communications; support requests; device, log, diagnostic and usage data; and preferences or consent records. We do not intend to store full payment-card details; payment information is handled by the payment provider under its own terms.

3. How we use data
We use personal data to create and secure accounts; display products and retailer information; process orders and payments; coordinate delivery, retailer settlement, cancellations and refunds; provide customer support; prevent fraud and abuse; moderate listings; maintain records; improve reliability and user experience; comply with legal obligations; and send marketing communications where permitted. You can opt out of promotional communications where applicable, but essential service messages may still be sent.

4. Lawful basis and fairness
We process data for purposes such as performing a contract, complying with legal obligations, legitimate interests pursued in a proportionate way, and consent where required. We aim to collect only data reasonably needed for the stated purposes and to handle it fairly and transparently in line with the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023 and other applicable requirements.

5. When data is shared
We may share relevant information with the retailer fulfilling your order (for example, recipient name, delivery address and phone number), payment providers such as Paystack, delivery partners, hosting and technology providers, customer-support tools, professional advisers, regulators or law-enforcement bodies where legally required, and a successor in a lawful business transfer. We do not permit retailers to use customer delivery details for unrelated marketing. We do not sell personal data as a business model.

6. International transfers
Some service providers may process data outside Nigeria. Where this happens, we will take steps required by applicable law to ensure an appropriate level of protection and lawful transfer arrangements.

7. Retention and security
We retain data for as long as reasonably needed for the purposes described, including order administration, accounting, dispute resolution, security and legal compliance. Retention periods depend on the data type and legal obligations. We use reasonable technical and organisational safeguards, but no internet service can guarantee absolute security. Please protect your password and promptly report suspected account misuse.

8. Your rights
Subject to applicable law and any lawful exceptions, you may have rights to request access to your personal data, correction, deletion, restriction or objection to certain processing, data portability, withdrawal of consent, and to lodge a complaint with the Nigeria Data Protection Commission. To make a request, contact Support@barristerstreet.org. We may need to verify your identity before responding.

9. Children
SEEK is not designed for children to make independent purchases where they lack legal capacity. If you believe a child has provided personal data unlawfully, contact us so we can assess and take appropriate action.

10. Cookies and similar technologies
SEEK may use essential cookies or local storage to maintain sessions, security, cart state and preferences. If analytics or advertising technologies are added, we will provide appropriate notices and obtain consent where required.

11. Changes and contact
We may update this policy as our services or legal obligations change. The latest version will be published on SEEK with an updated effective date. Privacy requests and questions: Support@barristerstreet.org.

Operator: BSN Consulting Limited. This policy should be reviewed by a qualified Nigerian privacy professional before launch.
$seek_privacy$, updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'privacy';

UPDATE policies SET title = 'Returns & Refunds Policy', body = $seek_returns$
Effective date: 16 October 2026

1. Our approach
SEEK is a marketplace operated by BSN Consulting Limited. Retailers are responsible for the products they supply; SEEK oversees the marketplace complaint and refund process and coordinates with the retailer and payment provider. This policy does not limit rights that consumers have under applicable Nigerian law.

2. When to contact us
Contact Support@barristerstreet.org as soon as reasonably possible after delivery or discovery of a problem. Include your order reference, the product, the reason for the request and clear photos or other evidence where relevant. The product page or checkout may state product-specific return conditions and a request window. If no window is displayed, contact us promptly; we will assess the request under applicable law and the circumstances rather than treating silence as a waiver of legal rights.

3. Potentially eligible reasons
Requests may be considered where an item is damaged, defective, materially different from its description, incorrect, incomplete, or not delivered. Change-of-mind returns may depend on the product listing, retailer terms, condition of the item and applicable law. Items must not be misused or damaged by the customer. Hygiene-sensitive, perishable, personalised, digital or other specially regulated products may have lawful restrictions, but those restrictions cannot remove mandatory statutory remedies.

4. How the process works
Submit a request through customer support with the relevant evidence. SEEK may ask the retailer or delivery partner for information and may provide instructions for return or inspection. Do not send an item to an address that has not been confirmed by SEEK or the retailer. The outcome may be a repair, replacement, partial refund, full refund or other remedy appropriate under the law and facts. We will communicate the decision and next steps.

5. Refund method and timing
Approved refunds are generally returned through the original payment method where supported by the payment provider. The time it takes for funds to appear may depend on the provider and the customer's bank. We will not describe a refund as completed until it has been submitted or recorded as completed in the relevant payment process. If the original method is unavailable, we will contact the customer to agree a lawful alternative.

6. Cancellations
Cancellation may be possible before a retailer has begun fulfilment or dispatched the order. Once an order is in preparation or transit, cancellation may require a return or delivery refusal process. Nothing here limits any cancellation right required by law.

7. Delivery costs and deductions
Responsibility for return delivery costs will depend on the reason for return, the disclosed terms and applicable law. We will not impose an unlawful fee or deduction. Any permitted deduction will be explained before it is applied.

8. Abuse and disputes
We may decline a request where evidence reasonably shows fraud, misuse or a request outside applicable eligibility rules, but will explain the decision and consider relevant evidence. Customers can ask SEEK to review a decision and may pursue remedies available through competent consumer-protection bodies or courts.

Contact: Support@barristerstreet.org. Operator: BSN Consulting Limited.

The final product-specific timelines and operational refund procedures should be reviewed by Nigerian counsel and aligned with the live payment provider configuration before launch.
$seek_returns$, updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'returns';

UPDATE policies SET title = 'Delivery Policy', body = $seek_delivery$
Effective date: 16 October 2026

1. Delivery model
SEEK is a marketplace operated by BSN Consulting Limited. Depending on the order, delivery may be arranged by SEEK, the retailer or a third-party delivery partner. The responsible party and any delivery charge or estimate will be shown at checkout or communicated before the order is confirmed where the system requires a delivery quote.

2. Coverage and charges
Delivery availability, fees and estimated times depend on the product, retailer, destination and delivery method. Do not assume that every product can be delivered to every location. Where a delivery charge cannot be calculated at checkout, SEEK may contact you or provide a quote before payment is completed. No undisclosed delivery charge should be added after confirmation without your agreement or a lawful basis.

3. Processing and estimated times
Retailers may need time to confirm stock, prepare and package an order. Estimated delivery windows are estimates unless expressly guaranteed. Delays may arise from weather, traffic, public holidays, security conditions, inaccurate address details, carrier disruption or events outside reasonable control. We will use reasonable efforts to communicate material delays.

4. Multiple retailers
An order containing products from multiple retailers may arrive in separate packages and at different times. Each retailer's fulfilment status may be tracked separately. Delivery of one package does not mean all items in the order have been delivered.

5. Customer responsibilities
Provide a complete address, a working phone number and any useful delivery instructions. Ensure someone authorised can receive the order. If delivery fails because information is inaccurate or no recipient is available, redelivery or additional charges may apply only where disclosed and lawful. Do not share verification codes with anyone except through a process expressly provided by SEEK or the delivery provider.

6. Receipt and problems
Check the package and items as soon as reasonably possible. If an item is missing, damaged, incorrect or appears tampered with, contact Support@barristerstreet.org promptly with the order reference and evidence. Please retain packaging where practical until the issue is resolved. This request to report promptly does not remove statutory consumer rights.

7. Failed delivery and returns
If delivery cannot be completed, SEEK or the retailer may contact you to arrange another attempt, collection or cancellation. Any return to sender, redelivery fee or refund will be handled under the order terms, the Returns & Refunds Policy and applicable law.

8. Contact
For delivery questions, contact Support@barristerstreet.org and include your order reference. Operator: BSN Consulting Limited.

Before launch, SEEK should confirm its delivery coverage, carrier contracts, fee configuration and escalation process so public estimates accurately reflect operational capability.
$seek_delivery$, updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'delivery';

UPDATE policies SET title = 'Prohibited Products Policy', body = $seek_prohibited$
Effective date: 16 October 2026

1. Purpose
SEEK, operated by BSN Consulting Limited, aims to provide a lawful and trustworthy marketplace. Retailers may list only products they are legally entitled to sell and that comply with applicable Nigerian laws, regulations, product-safety requirements and this policy.

2. Prohibited or restricted listings
Unless expressly permitted under a lawful, verified category-specific process, retailers must not list:
• Illegal drugs, controlled substances, drug paraphernalia or products making unlawful medical claims.
• Prescription-only medicines, unregistered medicines, counterfeit medicines or medical products that require authorisation the seller does not hold.
• Firearms, ammunition, explosives, prohibited weapons, weapon components or unlawful weapon accessories.
• Counterfeit, pirated, stolen, fraudulently obtained or intellectual-property-infringing goods.
• Products made from protected wildlife, endangered species or unlawfully harvested natural resources.
• Human remains, organs, or products involving exploitation or non-consensual material.
• Stolen financial credentials, identity documents, personal data, surveillance tools intended for unlawful use, or products designed primarily to facilitate fraud or cyber abuse.
• Recalled, unsafe, adulterated, expired or unlawfully labelled products, including food, cosmetics, supplements and electrical goods.
• Tobacco, nicotine, alcohol, gambling services or other age-restricted goods where the sale or promotion is prohibited or the required age/authorisation controls are not available.
• Products or content that promote violence, exploitation, hate-based unlawful conduct or illegal activity.
• Any other item whose sale, advertising, possession, import, export or delivery is prohibited by applicable law.

3. Restricted categories and proof
Some products may be lawful only if the retailer holds licences, registrations, safety certifications, age checks or other approvals. SEEK may require documentation before allowing a listing and may decline a category where it cannot reasonably verify compliance. Uploading documents does not guarantee approval.

4. Retailer obligations
Retailers must provide accurate descriptions, authentic images, correct safety information, required warnings, valid expiry dates where applicable, and evidence of lawful sourcing when requested. Retailers must promptly remove or correct a listing if a product becomes recalled, unsafe or unlawful. Retailers must not manipulate reviews or misrepresent brand authorisation.

5. Reporting and enforcement
Customers and other users can report a suspected violation to Support@barristerstreet.org. SEEK may hide, reject or remove listings; request documents; restrict sales; cancel orders; withhold settlement only where contractually and legally permitted; suspend or terminate retailer access; and refer suspected unlawful activity to relevant authorities. We may act urgently where safety, fraud or legal compliance requires it.

6. No exhaustive list
This policy is not an exhaustive catalogue of every restricted product or legal requirement. Retailers remain responsible for checking the laws and regulatory requirements applicable to their products, locations and customers. SEEK may update this policy as risks and requirements change.

Contact: Support@barristerstreet.org. Operator: BSN Consulting Limited.
$seek_prohibited$, updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'prohibited';

UPDATE policies SET title = 'Retailer Agreement', body = $seek_retailer_agreement$
Effective date: 16 October 2026

This Retailer Agreement is between BSN Consulting Limited ("SEEK", "we") and the retailer applying to sell through the SEEK marketplace ("Retailer", "you"). By submitting a retailer application, accepting this Agreement electronically or using retailer tools after acceptance, you agree to these terms.

1. Approval and account information
Retailer access is subject to review and approval. You must provide accurate business, identity, contact, banking and registration information requested by SEEK and promptly update changes. Approval is not a government licence or a guarantee of sales. Keep account credentials secure and ensure only authorised staff use the account.

2. Independent retailer
You operate as an independent seller and are responsible for your business, products, staff, taxes, permits, warranties and legal compliance. This Agreement does not create employment, partnership, franchise or agency authority beyond the limited marketplace and payment arrangements expressly described. You may not claim SEEK manufactures or endorses your products unless authorised in writing.

3. Listings, stock and fulfilment
You must ensure that every listing is accurate, current, lawful and not misleading. Keep prices, stock, specifications, images, delivery estimates, product condition and warranty details up to date. Accept and fulfil orders promptly, package goods safely, honour confirmed prices, communicate delays and maintain evidence of dispatch and delivery. Do not substitute products or impose undisclosed charges without the customer's agreement.

4. Product safety and prohibited goods
You are solely responsible for ensuring that products are authentic, safe, properly labelled and legally sold. You must comply with SEEK's Prohibited Products Policy and provide licences, registrations, test reports or sourcing records when reasonably requested. You must promptly notify SEEK of recalls, safety incidents or regulatory action affecting your listings.

5. Commission and other fees
SEEK's proposed launch model includes free basic retailer registration and a standard commission initially proposed at 8% of eligible completed product sales. The actual applicable commission, any category-specific rate, the calculation base, taxes and any other deduction must be shown in your retailer dashboard or a separate commercial schedule before it applies. If a different rate is shown in an accepted written agreement or dashboard notice, that disclosed rate governs the relevant transactions. SEEK will not apply an undisclosed fee retroactively to an already completed order. Optional paid advertising, featured storefronts, premium subscriptions or paid listing packages will be charged only after their prices and terms are disclosed and accepted.

6. Payments and settlement
Customers pay through SEEK checkout using Paystack or another payment method offered. SEEK records the order, payment and retailer balance and coordinates settlement under the disclosed payment arrangement. Retailer settlement eligibility may depend on verified payment, fulfilment/delivery confirmation, applicable return or dispute checks, fraud review and payment-provider or legal requirements. The actual settlement schedule and any lawful reserves or adjustments will be communicated in the dashboard or commercial schedule; this Agreement does not promise an unconfirmed fixed payout time. SEEK will provide transaction records sufficient to explain commission and adjustments.

7. Refunds, cancellations and chargebacks
You must cooperate promptly with customer complaints, returns, replacements and refunds. Responsibility for product defects, misdescription, incorrect items and retailer-caused fulfilment failures rests with you, subject to applicable law and the specific facts. Refunds, chargebacks, cancellations and delivery failures may adjust the retailer balance in accordance with the disclosed settlement rules. SEEK will provide a reason for material adjustments where reasonably practicable. No clause authorises unlawful withholding or removes a customer's statutory rights.

8. Customer data
Use customer information only to process and fulfil the relevant order, provide necessary after-sales service and meet legal obligations. Do not sell customer data, add customers to unrelated marketing lists, contact them outside legitimate order purposes, or retain information longer than needed. Apply appropriate security and promptly notify SEEK of suspected unauthorised access or disclosure. Comply with applicable data-protection law.

9. Advertising and promotions
Paid promotional products, banners or storefront placements must be clearly identified as sponsored where appropriate. You must not make false claims, manipulate search or reviews, misuse another party's intellectual property, or offer promotions you cannot honour. Advertising prices, duration, placement and cancellation terms will be disclosed before purchase.

10. Records, tax and indemnity
Maintain accurate records of sales, stock, product sourcing, licences, taxes and fulfilment. You are responsible for your taxes and statutory obligations. To the extent permitted by law, you are responsible for losses, claims or costs arising from your breach, unlawful products, negligence, infringement or misleading listing, except to the extent caused by SEEK's own breach or unlawful conduct.

11. Monitoring and suspension
SEEK may review listings and retailer performance, request information, remove or restrict listings, pause orders or suspend accounts where reasonably necessary for safety, suspected fraud, non-fulfilment, repeated complaints, legal compliance or breach of this Agreement. Where appropriate, we will give reasons and an opportunity to respond. Urgent action may be taken first where needed to protect users or comply with law.

12. Term and termination
Either party may request termination by contacting the other, subject to completion of pending orders, customer remedies, refunds, lawful records retention and outstanding balances. SEEK may terminate for serious or repeated breach or legal necessity. Termination does not remove obligations that arose before termination.

13. Changes and disputes
SEEK may update this Agreement with notice of material changes. Changes to commission or fees apply prospectively after disclosure and acceptance where required. The laws of the Federal Republic of Nigeria govern this Agreement, and disputes are subject to competent Nigerian courts. Contact Support@barristerstreet.org for retailer support or a complaint.

Operator: BSN Consulting Limited.

This Agreement is a business draft and must be reviewed by qualified Nigerian counsel before retailer onboarding. Confirm payment-provider permissions and the final settlement schedule before enabling live retailer payouts.
$seek_retailer_agreement$, updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'retailer-agreement';

