Retailers may need time to confirm stock, prepare and package an order. Estimated delivery windows are estimates unless expressly guaranteed. Delays may arise from weather, traffic, public holidays, security conditions, inaccurate address details, carrier disruption or events outside reasonable control. We will use reasonable efforts to communicate material delays.

4. Multiple retailers
An order containing products from multiple retailers may arrive in separate packages and at different times. Each retailer's fulfilment status may be tracked separately. Delivery of one package does not mean all items in the order have been delivered.

5. Customer responsibilities
Provide a complete address, a working phone number and any useful delivery instructions. Ensure someone authorised can receive the order. If delivery fails because information is inaccurate or no recipient is available, redelivery or additional charges may apply only where disclosed and lawful. Do not share verification codes with anyone except through a process expressly provided by SEEK or the delivery provider.

6. Receipt and problems
Check the package and items as soon as reasonably possible. If an item is missing, damaged, incorrect or appears tampered with, contact Support@barristerstreet.org promptly with the order reference and evidence. Please retain packaging where practical until the issue is resolved. This request to report promptly does not remove statutory consumer rights.

7. Failed delivery and returns
If delivery cannot be completed, SEEK or the retailer may contact you to arrange another attempt, collection or cancellation. Any return to sender, redelivery fee or refund will be handled under the order terms, the Returns & Refunds Policy and applicable law.

8. Contact
For delivery questions, contact Support@barristerstreet.org and include your order reference. Operator: BSN Consulting Limited.

Before launch, SEEK should confirm its delivery coverage, carrier contracts, fee configuration and escalation process so public estimates accurately reflect operational capability.
$insert_delivery$) ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO policies (slug, title, body) VALUES ('prohibited', 'Prohibited Products Policy', $insert_prohibited$
Effective date: 16 October 2026

1. Purpose
SEEK, operated by BSN Consulting Limited, aims to provide a lawful and trustworthy marketplace. Retailers may list only products they are legally entitled to sell and that comply with applicable Nigerian laws, regulations, product-safety requirements and this policy.

2. Prohibited or restricted listings
Unless expressly permitted under a lawful, verified category-specific process, retailers must not list:
• Illegal drugs, controlled substances, drug paraphernalia or products making unlawful medical claims.
• Prescription-only medicines, unregistered medicines, counterfeit medicines or medical products that require authorisation the seller does not hold.
• Firearms, ammunition, explosives, prohibited weapons, weapon components or unlawful weapon accessories.
• Counterfeit, pirated, stolen, fraudulently obtained or intellectual-property-infringing goods.
• Products made from protected wildlife, endangered species or unlawfully harvested natural resources.
• Human remains, organs, or products involving exploitation or non-consensual material.
• Stolen financial credentials, identity documents, personal data, surveillance tools intended for unlawful use, or products designed primarily to facilitate fraud or cyber abuse.
• Recalled, unsafe, adulterated, expired or unlawfully labelled products, including food, cosmetics, supplements and electrical goods.
• Tobacco, nicotine, alcohol, gambling services or other age-restricted goods where the sale or promotion is prohibited or the required age/authorisation controls are not available.
• Products or content that promote violence, exploitation, hate-based unlawful conduct or illegal activity.
• Any other item whose sale, advertising, possession, import, export or delivery is prohibited by applicable law.

3. Restricted categories and proof
Some products may be lawful only if the retailer holds licences, registrations, safety certifications, age checks or other approvals. SEEK may require documentation before allowing a listing and may decline a category where it cannot reasonably verify compliance. Uploading documents does not guarantee approval.

4. Retailer obligations
Retailers must provide accurate descriptions, authentic images, correct safety information, required warnings, valid expiry dates where applicable, and evidence of lawful sourcing when requested. Retailers must promptly remove or correct a listing if a product becomes recalled, unsafe or unlawful. Retailers must not manipulate reviews or misrepresent brand authorisation.

5. Reporting and enforcement
Customers and other users can report a suspected violation to Support@barristerstreet.org. SEEK may hide, reject or remove listings; request documents; restrict sales; cancel orders; withhold settlement only where contractually and legally permitted; suspend or terminate retailer access; and refer suspected unlawful activity to relevant authorities. We may act urgently where safety, fraud or legal compliance requires it.

6. No exhaustive list
This policy is not an exhaustive catalogue of every restricted product or legal requirement. Retailers remain responsible for checking the laws and regulatory requirements applicable to their products, locations and customers. SEEK may update this policy as risks and requirements change.

Contact: Support@barristerstreet.org. Operator: BSN Consulting Limited.
$insert_prohibited$) ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO policies (slug, title, body) VALUES ('retailer-agreement', 'Retailer Agreement', $insert_retailer_agreement$
Effective date: 16 October 2026

This Retailer Agreement is between BSN Consulting Limited ("SEEK", "we") and the retailer applying to sell through the SEEK marketplace ("Retailer", "you"). By submitting a retailer application, accepting this Agreement electronically or using retailer tools after acceptance, you agree to these terms.

1. Approval and account information
Retailer access is subject to review and approval. You must provide accurate business, identity, contact, banking and registration information requested by SEEK and promptly update changes. Approval is not a government licence or a guarantee of sales. Keep account credentials secure and ensure only authorised staff use the account.

2. Independent retailer
You operate as an independent seller and are responsible for your business, products, staff, taxes, permits, warranties and legal compliance. This Agreement does not create employment, partnership, franchise or agency authority beyond the limited marketplace and payment arrangements expressly described. You may not claim SEEK manufactures or endorses your products unless authorised in writing.

3. Listings, stock and fulfilment
You must ensure that every listing is accurate, current, lawful and not misleading. Keep prices, stock, specifications, images, delivery estimates, product condition and warranty details up to date. Accept and fulfil orders promptly, package goods safely, honour confirmed prices, communicate delays and maintain evidence of dispatch and delivery. Do not substitute products or impose undisclosed charges without the customer's agreement.

4. Product safety and prohibited goods
You are solely responsible for ensuring that products are authentic, safe, properly labelled and legally sold. You must comply with SEEK's Prohibited Products Policy and provide licences, registrations, test reports or sourcing records when reasonably requested. You must promptly notify SEEK of recalls, safety incidents or regulatory action affecting your listings.

5. Commission and other fees
SEEK's proposed launch model includes free basic retailer registration and a standard commission initially proposed at 8% of eligible completed product sales. The actual applicable commission, any category-specific rate, the calculation base, taxes and any other deduction must be shown in your retailer dashboard or a separate commercial schedule before it applies. If a different rate is shown in an accepted written agreement or dashboard notice, that disclosed rate governs the relevant transactions. SEEK will not apply an undisclosed fee retroactively to an already completed order. Optional paid advertising, featured storefronts, premium subscriptions or paid listing packages will be charged only after their prices and terms are disclosed and accepted.

6. Payments and settlement
Customers pay through SEEK checkout using Paystack or another payment method offered. SEEK records the order, payment and retailer balance and coordinates settlement under the disclosed payment arrangement. Retailer settlement eligibility may depend on verified payment, fulfilment/delivery confirmation, applicable return or dispute checks, fraud review and payment-provider or legal requirements. The actual settlement schedule and any lawful reserves or adjustments will be communicated in the dashboard or commercial schedule; this Agreement does not promise an unconfirmed fixed payout time. SEEK will provide transaction records sufficient to explain commission and adjustments.

7. Refunds, cancellations and chargebacks
You must cooperate promptly with customer complaints, returns, replacements and refunds. Responsibility for product defects, misdescription, incorrect items and retailer-caused fulfilment failures rests with you, subject to applicable law and the specific facts. Refunds, chargebacks, cancellations and delivery failures may adjust the retailer balance in accordance with the disclosed settlement rules. SEEK will provide a reason for material adjustments where reasonably practicable. No clause authorises unlawful withholding or removes a customer's statutory rights.

8. Customer data
Use customer information only to process and fulfil the relevant order, provide necessary after-sales service and meet legal obligations. Do not sell customer data, add customers to unrelated marketing lists, contact them outside legitimate order purposes, or retain information longer than needed. Apply appropriate security and promptly notify SEEK of suspected unauthorised access or disclosure. Comply with applicable data-protection law.

9. Advertising and promotions
Paid promotional products, banners or storefront placements must be clearly identified as sponsored where appropriate. You must not make false claims, manipulate search or reviews, misuse another party's intellectual property, or offer promotions you cannot honour. Advertising prices, duration, placement and cancellation terms will be disclosed before purchase.

10. Records, tax and indemnity
Maintain accurate records of sales, stock, product sourcing, licences, taxes and fulfilment. You are responsible for your taxes and statutory obligations. To the extent permitted by law, you are responsible for losses, claims or costs arising from your breach, unlawful products, negligence, infringement or misleading listing, except to the extent caused by SEEK's own breach or unlawful conduct.

11. Monitoring and suspension
SEEK may review listings and retailer performance, request information, remove or restrict listings, pause orders or suspend accounts where reasonably necessary for safety, suspected fraud, non-fulfilment, repeated complaints, legal compliance or breach of this Agreement. Where appropriate, we will give reasons and an opportunity to respond. Urgent action may be taken first where needed to protect users or comply with law.

12. Term and termination
Either party may request termination by contacting the other, subject to completion of pending orders, customer remedies, refunds, lawful records retention and outstanding balances. SEEK may terminate for serious or repeated breach or legal necessity. Termination does not remove obligations that arose before termination.

13. Changes and disputes
SEEK may update this Agreement with notice of material changes. Changes to commission or fees apply prospectively after disclosure and acceptance where required. The laws of the Federal Republic of Nigeria govern this Agreement, and disputes are subject to competent Nigerian courts. Contact Support@barristerstreet.org for retailer support or a complaint.

Operator: BSN Consulting Limited.

This Agreement is a business draft and must be reviewed by qualified Nigerian counsel before retailer onboarding. Confirm payment-provider permissions and the final settlement schedule before enabling live retailer payouts.
$insert_retailer_agreement$) ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

